  "finalText": "I built the \"Pulse 2\" title sequence in the Main composition: 10 s, 1920×1080, 30 fps, on a near-black `#0B0B0D` background with electric orange `#FF5A1F` as the accent. The critic scores it 87/100.\n\n- **Feature words (0.5–3.5 s):** \"40h battery\", \"Spatial audio\", \"Pure silence\" each hold for two beats at 120 BPM (1 s each). Each cut lands on a beat and fires a full-frame orange flash that snaps out in about 0.16 s. Each word enters with a 125% → 100% Expo Out punch and cuts hard on exit.\n- **Product name (3.5 s):** **PULSE 2** slams in from 180% to 100% with Expo Out. A thin orange shockwave ring expands from behind it and fades by 4.2 s. An orange rule draws out under the name at 4.0 s to fill the gap before the next beat.\n- **Available now (7.0 s):** an orange pill with dark text springs in at the 7.0 s beat and holds to the end.\n\nMarkers sit on the cut beats (0.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 7.0 s). I didn't add any audio, since you didn't ask for a music track. The cuts are on the 120 BPM grid by design, so if you add a track, the timing will need checking against its actual beats.\n\nPossible next tweaks: a second ring on the 7.0 s pill beat, a wipe transition instead of the flash, or a larger pill with more padding."
